    {
      "chapter": "Print layout and assembly order",
      "duration_ms": 1800,
      "note": "The screw prints on its through-axis flat. Stand the nut on its end, and put the jaw and keeper on their broad end faces. Five separated parts fit within 204 by 166 mm, including the conservative 235.5 by 256 mm dual-tool bed. Insert the nut, turn in the screw, slide on the jaw and secure the keeper with its M3 hardware. The frame's 45-degree bore roof preserves the circular rotating envelope without a horizontal bridge."
    },
